      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-133934",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/87/87f2b3e0804faf3109308a17eea3d04078b91c1210b46d6ed8bba1cc2d0b80e6.png)\n\nEach week, the admin of a local hospital adds up the number of heatstroke cases and swimming pool injuries. The results are shown in the scatter plot above. Which of the following is most likely true?\n\n1. An increase in the number of heatstroke cases causes an increase in swimming pool injuries.\n2. An increase in the number of swimming pool injuries causes an increase in heatstroke cases.\n3. Hotter weather influences the number of heatstroke cases and swimming pool injuries."
